# Scene 4: built on CsCheck. stage/cscheck.html, full bleed: CsCheck's engine underneath, what Entities adds on top
# (first-class properties, nine axes, AutoTest), the rules as discoverable properties, and the one line that runs them.
Import //reels/entities.reelpreset
Open ../stage/cscheck.html

Output //.artifacts/reel/scenes/04-one-line.mp4
Set Browser chromium
Set Viewport 1600x900
Set Cursor off
Set ClickRipples off
Set WaitTimeout 20s

Hide
Wait css:"#next"
Sleep 1s
Open ../stage/cscheck.html
Wait css:"#layers.on"
Show
Say@skeptic "I already do property testing. I use CsCheck."
Say@over "Good. Entities is built on CsCheck: its generators, its shrinking, its seeds. On top, it adds [e1] first-class properties, [e2] nine axes, [e3] and AutoTest. [done]"
Wait [e1]
Click css:"#next"
Wait [e2]
Click css:"#next"
Wait [e3]
Click css:"#next"
Wait [done]
Sleep 800ms

Click css:"#next"
Say@over "Every rule you declare is a named property with a shape, [shape] and the shape says which questions to ask. [all] A source generator gathers them, so nothing is written twice."
Wait [shape]
Click css:"#next"
Wait [all]
Click css:"#next"
Sleep 2s

Click css:"#next"
Say@over "Then one line: [rules] your rules and your CsCheck generator. [ops] It finds the operations on the type, [axes] and runs every axis the rules declare. [kept] Every failure is shrunk by CsCheck, with a seed to replay it."
Wait [rules]
Click css:"#next"
Wait [ops]
Click css:"#next"
Wait [axes]
Click css:"#next"
Wait [kept]
Click css:"#next"
Sleep 2500ms
Say@skeptic "And a rule I add next month?"
Say "Found, and tested. No new test code."
Sleep 500ms
